From: thor <thor@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: thor: drive the LRA haptics as an LRA

PB-OS's qcs8550-ayn-thor.append (project-barry/pb-os 8ea4653), as a patch
against Armada's Thor device tree.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
index f5b63a52e..d48c300df 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -479,3 +479,13 @@ &spk_amp_l {
 &spk_amp_r {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8550/ayn/thor/aw883xx_acf.bin";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The body's vibration motor is an LRA, driven as stock Android does (AYN's Thor
+ * device tree: no ERM mode, 1300 mV). The common ERM setup at 5000 mV feeds it
+ * plain DC, so rumble was a single click (PB-OS, tested on a Thor: its issue #8).
+ */
+&pm8550b_hv_haptics {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,use-erm;
+	qcom,vmax-mv = <1300>;
+};
